# Cargo build artifacts.
# Use `target/` (not `/target/`) so the rule catches nested workspaces too
# — `crates/probes/` is a separate workspace whose target/ is multi-GB.
target/

# Don't commit Cargo.lock (any workspace, any depth). A committed lock pins git
# deps to dev-history commits and crates.io deps to specific releases, which go
# stale as we develop. Tracking branch tips / latest matching releases keeps the
# dependency landscape current rather than expiring on a pin.
Cargo.lock

# Probes are throwaway experiments in a separate workspace. Ignore probe content
# so it never clutters git status or lands in a `git add -A` (the multi-GB
# p2panda / willow clones live here). Already-committed probes stay tracked;
# `git add -f` to keep a new one, `git rm --cached` to drop one.
/crates/probes/

# Backup / swap files
**/*.rs.bk
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# IDE / editor configs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Coverage / profiling output
*.profraw
*.profdata
flamegraph.svg
perf.data*

# Test / debug log directories (project convention: logs go here, not
# alongside source). No leading slash so the rule catches these dirs at any
# depth (e.g. crates/*/.cargo-check-logs/), not just the repo root.
logs/
.test-logs/
.cargo-check-logs/

# Local scratch and verification artifacts. These runs can contain logs,
# screenshots, session state, comms stores, and diagnostics dumps that are
# machine-local and should never be published from the repo.
/.tmp/
/target-codex/
/diagnostics-dump.txt

# Locally-downloaded model weights (e.g. all-MiniLM-L6-v2 fetched via
# `huggingface_hub.snapshot_download` for intelligence-embeddings BERT
# validation). Multi-MB binaries; do not commit. Devs set MERE_MINILM_DIR
# to point at this directory after running the download recipe in
# crates/intelligence-embeddings/README.md.
/models/

# Host session store — runtime artifact written by `cargo run -p host`
# (./mere-sessions relative to the run cwd). Never commit session state.
mere-sessions/

# Local tooling cache (semantic index / scratch db). Multi-MB binary cache,
# not source — never commit.
.sem/

# Python helper bytecode is local tooling output.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local cargo path overrides (genet/netrender local working copies) - local-dev only.
# The .example is committed: it documents the sibling-checkout edit loop and its
# paths are relative, so it is copyable as-is. The live file stays ignored so a
# clean clone still resolves the owned repos from GitHub and builds standalone.
# Two constraints fight here. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so a bare `.cargo/` makes the negation below silently dead. But a
# pattern containing a slash is anchored to THIS file's directory, so a bare
# `.cargo/*` would stop ignoring nested ones (ports/graphshell/web/.cargo/).
# `**/.cargo/*` excludes the contents at every level without excluding the dirs.
**/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/config.toml.example
/target-*/

# Isolated cargo homes created for dependency experiments — e.g.
# `.cargo-conatus-rapier-test/`, used on 2026-08-24 to resolve conatus against
# rapier in a clean resolver. Each holds a full git checkout cache: thousands of
# vendored files, including entire upstream test suites (that one carried a WPT
# checkout). A `git add -A` sweeps every one of them into the commit, which is
# how this rule came to be written. Ignore the class rather than the one name.
.cargo-*/

# Local host receipts can contain machine addresses, key fingerprints, and
# endpoint reachability details. Keep the raw resident-host rehearsal local.
ports/graphshell/docs/2026-07-28_h4f_resident_device_host_receipt.md

# The Circuit recipe's workspace graph is derived from `cargo metadata` by
# `ports/distillery/tests/walk_fixtures.rs`, not authored. A committed copy
# fell a generation behind every time a member was added (2026-09-03).
ports/distillery/tests/fixtures/circuit/
